Zero-Spend Budget 

Step-by-Step: Creating a Zero-Spend Budget Template

Log in to AWS Management Console:
Sign in to your account with your Root User credentials.

Navigate to AWS Budgets:
Open the Billing and Cost Management console.
In the left menu under Budgets and Planning, click Budgets.

Select the Template Option:
Click the Create budget button.
Under Budget setup, select Use a template (simplified).

Choose "Zero spend budget":
Under the Templates section, select Zero spend budget.
This pre-configured template tracks all AWS services and triggers an alert if your actual spend exceeds $0.01.

Configure Notification Email:
Enter a descriptive Budget name (or keep the default provided name).
Under Email recipients, type the primary email address where you want to receive alerts.

Create Budget:
Click Create budget at the bottom of the page to finalize.

Why Use This Template?
Zero Configuration Needed: Unlike custom cost budgets, you do not need to manually calculate thresholds, pick time periods, or select scope filters.

Instant Protection: You will receive an immediate email notification as soon as any unattached resource (such as an idle NAT Gateway, unattached Elastic IP or unexpected storage charge) incurs even a fraction of a cent.
